# Favicon & app icons (must)

Every landing project must use the **brand logo** as favicon. Never leave the Create Next App / Next.js default icon.

## Required files

| File | Size guide | Role |
|------|------------|------|
| `src/app/icon.png` | ~512×512 | App Router favicon (auto) |
| `src/app/apple-icon.png` | ~180×180 | Apple touch |
| `public/favicon.png` | 32×32 | Explicit `/favicon.png` |
| `public/apple-icon.png` | ~180×180 | Metadata / fallback |

## Build steps

1. Source: brand logo from `public/<pack>/logos/` (navbar mark)
2. Resize with `sharp` (or similar): square canvas, **transparent** pad (not cream plate)
3. Prefer transparent PNG so browser tabs do not show a cream/grey box behind the mark
4. Delete any default `src/app/favicon.ico` from the Next starter
5. Point `icons` in metadata (`@/lib/seo` / `layout`) at `/favicon.png` + apple icon
6. Keep file sizes tiny (favicon ≤ ~5KB; icon ≤ ~100KB)

## Never

- Ship the black/white Next.js triangle favicon
- Use the full-resolution navbar PNG (1MB+) as favicon
- Hotlink a remote favicon
- Bake a solid cream/grey rectangle behind the mark (shows as a box in Chrome tabs)

## Any landing

Swap logo source via `naturavive-brand.mdc` / `@/config/brand`. Same paths and rule.
